A||N||7||NOS3800||3800 Fieros Wreck Havoc at Import Drags||||10||
Z||000000||NOS3800||09-03-2001||03:41 PM||||Well, not really. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  My brother (SC3800) and I(NOS injected NA3800) decided at the last minute to race at the local import drag day here in southern Maryland. They allow sport compact domestics. We got classed into Pro 6: V6 powered cars with NOS, Turbo, or Supecharger. This meant that we were thrown in with Mazda RX7 turbos and Supra twin turbos. Out of the twenty cars in the class, we were the only non RX7 or Supra. They were all the late models except one 85 Mazda RX7 rotary that ran 13.00. Well, it was a Quick 8 class which meant only the quickest 8 get to race for the money, everyone else could compete in the E/T class which grouped ALL the non Quick 8 competitors(ie the slower cars). <BR>Well, Lildvil and I could only manage to qualify 9-10 in the class. My best of 13.43 and his best (in qualifying) was a 13.51, he ran a couple of 13.2's before qualifying. This race was held during the day on Sunday and temps were in the low 80's. We both had a REAL hard time with tire spin all day which was unusual at this track. The only thing we could figure was cause of all the FWD cars all the rubber being laid down was not under our rear wheels. The Supras and RX7's were pulling 12's and even 11's! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> Of course they were trailered in and they cost well over $60,000.<BR> Anyway, we didn't qualify for the Quick 8 and entered the E/T series and became the fastest cars in the class <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"> Lildvl made it to the final 6 and got beat by a 19 second Camry that ran dead on his dial in. I made it to the finals against the same Camry. I had a 13.43 dial-in but was running consistent 13.5's through eliminations. I should have changed the dial in to 13.5 but didn't have time cause once you ran you went straight back to the burnout box. So the motor had no time to cool and my NOS bottle was loosing pressure from all the runs (12 total). Well, I lost in the final, by .012 seconds. I gave up almost a 6 sec head start to the Camry. I still won 100 bucks so I was still happy.<BR>I was surprised how many people came up and took a peek at our cars. There was alot of interest. Especially since ours had full interiors and were street legal daily drivers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> oh and the chicks dug our cars!!<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.45@99.70 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||10
Z||000001||p-did||09-03-2001||04:26 PM||||Still not bad.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  At least yours aren't trailer queens.  <P>BTW: Where did you mount your nitrous bottle?  Front or rear?  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Jay Olson<BR>(AKA "fropuff")<BR>'86 GT, smashed rear fascia, fastback clip, right tail lamp assembly||||reg||1
